# SEO intelligence workspace - internal analytics only.
# Never deploy: dist/ is FTP-synced to production, and this holds exported
# analytics plus any credentials used to fetch it.
seo-intelligence/data/**/*.csv
seo-intelligence/data/**/*.tsv
seo-intelligence/data/**/*.xlsx
seo-intelligence/data/**/*.zip
seo-intelligence/**/credentials*.json
seo-intelligence/**/service-account*.json
seo-intelligence/**/*secret*
seo-intelligence/**/*token*
seo-intelligence/**/.env*

# Raw Search Console pulls taken from an authenticated session. Private: never
# commit. Sanitized summaries (data/gsc/gsc-summary-*.md) and reports stay tracked.
seo-intelligence/data/**/raw-*/
seo-intelligence/data/**/*.tsv

# Private infrastructure diagnostics. THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC.
#
# The DNS/TLS investigations record the owner's own network while diagnosing a
# fault that turned out to be ISP-side: public IP, LAN gateway address, gateway
# MAC/OUI and the ISP's MDU network name. The Bluehost support drafts name the
# backend server hostname and account-identifying details. None of that belongs
# in a public repository, and none of it is needed to build or run the site.
#
# These are untracked today only because nobody has run `git add` on them - no
# rule covered them, so a single `git add -A` would have published the owner's
# home network details. Matched by name so the directory as a whole stays
# committable: the 12 tracked SEO/release reports are unaffected, and a new
# report is only ignored if its name says it is one of these diagnostics.
seo-intelligence/reports/ssl-hsts-*.md
seo-intelligence/reports/dns-and-tls-*.md
seo-intelligence/reports/bluehost-*-request-*.md
# Scratch working directory for in-progress analysis.
seo-intelligence/reports/_work/

# visual QA artifacts (generated)
visual-qa-report.json
visual-qa-shots/
.playwright-mcp/
